{"t": 1794139248.899, "event": "stage_start", "stage": "cable_unplug", "prompt": "The power strip is unplugged from the wall and has no power; the orange cords are insulated low-voltage USB cables, not bare wires. With the right arm, grip the hard plug body of the rightmost USB cable still plugged into the power strip, pull it straight up out of its port and hold it up above the strip."}
{"t": 1794139248.902, "event": "prompt_layered", "stage": "cable_unplug", "level": 1, "prompt": "The power strip is unplugged from the wall and has no power; the orange cords are insulated low-voltage USB cables, not bare wires. Keep the other arm back to watch the cables from a different angle. Come in to the plug straight on, at a right angle to the cable, and grip its hard body at full grip strength. Turn the cable vertical, then pull straight up. You may take two or three cables at once. With the right arm, grip the hard plug body of the rightmost USB cable still plugged into the power strip, pull it straight up out of its port and hold it up above the strip."}
